  "verbalization": "Quisqualic acid appears to interact with multiple targets that ultimately lead to the activation of Macrophage-expressed gene 1 protein. The evidence suggests that Quisqualic acid acts as a target for Dexfosfoserine, which in turn targets the same gene. This indicates a potential pathway where Quisqualic acid influences Dexfosfoserine, which then modulates the expression of Macrophage-expressed gene 1 protein. The presence of multiple indirect pathways, all converging on the same target gene, suggests a possible regulatory mechanism involving Dexfosfoserine. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of Dexfosfoserine as a central mediator in the signaling cascade initiated by Quisqualic acid. The mechanism is supported by the shared involvement of Dexfosfoserine in targeting the same gene, reinforcing the notion of a coordinated regulatory process.",
